publish.py treated "no release yet" as a failure

A brand-new tag has no release, and the script asked GitHub for one to decide what to do: the
404 that means "not yet" was routed to the same die() as a 403 or a 500, so the first run of
release.sh for any new version died on the very check that tells it to create the release. 404
now raises NotFound, which is what main() was already catching - it just could never have seen
it raised.
